Three equalities hold: (1) the written JSON parses to exactly the five independently derived values; (2) the written bytes equal the canonical serialization of those five values (json.dumps(indent=1, sort_keys=True) + "\n"); (3) the written bytes equal the committed blob at the freeze rev, so the tool reproduces the instrument constant and does not merely agree with a working-tree copy.

Note (read side): --check grades the blob at --rev, not the working tree. With a sentinel in the worktree and the correct committed blob at the rev, --check still printed PINS_CHECK OK (observed on the cwd96 fixture). That is the intended binding: the pins being checked are the committed ones.
